   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In November 2024, we committed $20 million to Robust International, a trader of agri-commodities. This will support Robust to buy sesame and cashew nuts directly from cooperatives and farmers locally, as well as support operations and jobs at its new processing facilities in Burkina Faso, C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire, and Mozambique. It is expected to support over 1,100 jobs at the processing facilities and up to 600,000 smallholder farmers to improve their incomes. Our commitment was part of a $105 million facility in collaboration with FMO, Proparco, Swedfund and ILX.In September 2025, the facility was expanded from $105 million to $175 million, through additional commitments from Impact Fund Denmark, and Austria&apos;s OeEB, as well as an increased contribution from FMO. BII also committed an additional $5 million to the expanded facility.</narrative>
   </description>
